SafeBitez
=========

The MIT license in `LICENSE` covers the source code of this repository only.
It does not cover third-party data that the application downloads, imports,
queries, or displays. Those data keep their own licenses and rights, summarised
below. Nothing in this repository redistributes the downloaded datasets: they
are fetched at runtime or during an explicit import and stay out of version
control and the Docker build context (see the root `.gitignore` and
`backend/.dockerignore`).

IFCT reference data
-------------------
The Indian Food Composition Tables (IFCT 2017) reference values used by the
`ifct` importer are published under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 or later (AGPL-3.0-or-later). Redistributing the tables, or a
modified version of them, additionally requires the separate rights granted by
the source book publisher. This repository does not bundle the IFCT dataset;
`python -m app.importers ifct --download` fetches it on demand. Anyone who
redistributes imported IFCT data must comply with the AGPL and obtain the
publisher's separate rights.

Open Food Facts
---------------
Product records retrieved from Open Food Facts are made available under the
Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0. Attribution to Open Food Facts and
share-alike terms apply to derived databases. This repository stores only what
a user lookup or search fetches at runtime.

Network-fetched data in general
-------------------------------
Barcode lookups, product name searches, label-photo extraction, and dish
assessment send or retrieve data over the network. That fetched data is not
redistributed in this repository, and the terms of each upstream source govern
its use, attribution, and redistribution.
